{"ref":"BDB, כְּבָר²","hw":"כְּבָר²","html":"† II. <big><span dir=\"rtl\">כְּבָר</span></big>  <strong>n.pr.fl. Kĕbār</strong>, a river (or perhaps a canal) of Babylonia, not at present identified, by wh. the exiles, among whom Ez. ministered, were settled; always in the phr. <span dir=\"rtl\">נְהַר כְּבָר</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 1:1\" href=\"/Ezekiel.1.1\">Ez 1:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 1:3\" href=\"/Ezekiel.1.3\">3</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 3:15\" href=\"/Ezekiel.3.15\">3:15</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 3:23\" href=\"/Ezekiel.3.23\">23</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 10:15\" href=\"/Ezekiel.10.15\">10:15</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 10:20\" href=\"/Ezekiel.10.20\">20</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 10:22\" href=\"/Ezekiel.10.22\">22</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 43:3\" href=\"/Ezekiel.43.3\">43:3</a> (cf. Sm <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 1:1\" href=\"/Ezekiel.1.1\">Ez 1:1</a> Del<sup>Par. 47f., 184</sup>).","next":"BDB, כבר","prev":"BDB, כְּבָר"}